# /usr/share/w/defaults/home-subvols — per-account paths W keeps OUTSIDE @home
# snapshots, carved as nested btrfs subvolumes by `apply.sh --homesubvol`.
#
# W's own list. Do NOT edit: every update overwrites this file wholesale.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE
#
# State a toolchain keeps per user that is large, ephemeral and fully
# recoverable from the network — download caches, module caches, build caches.
# A rollback of @home should not drag gigabytes of it along, and a restore
# should not resurrect it. Config and project files never belong here: they
# are exactly what @home snapshots exist to protect.
#
# HOW IT IS APPLIED
#
# One line = one path relative to the account's home, carved for every human
# account (see w_home_users) — only while the path is still absent, because a
# populated directory cannot be turned into a subvolume in place. Accounts
# created later catch up on the next apply / w-sync. Off btrfs the path becomes
# a plain directory. A trailing `# tool: why` is the convention.
#
# ADDING A TOOL
#
# One line here; if the tool needs steering to land there (Go's GOPATH does),
# pair it with a login-shell env drop-in /etc/profile.d/w-<tool>.sh. No code.

.cache/uv       # uv: download cache (package-python.md)
.cache/pip      # pip: download cache
.cache/go       # go: GOMODCACHE + GOCACHE, routed here by /etc/profile.d/w-go.sh
